Hint:\(T=2\pi \sqrt{\frac{l}{g_{eff}}}\)

Step:Find the time period of the simple pendulum.
The time period of the simple pendulum in a stationary lift is given by;
\(T=2 \pi \sqrt{\frac{l}{g}} ~~~...(1)\)
The time period of the simple pendulum in a lift accelerates upwards is given
by;
\(\Rightarrow T^{\prime}=2 \pi \sqrt{\frac{l}{g _{eff}}} ~~~...(2)\)
The effective acceleration of the pendulum is given by;
\(g_{eff}=g+ \frac{g}{6}=\frac{7}{6}g\)
Divide equation \((2)\)by\((1)\) we get;
\(\Rightarrow \frac{T^{\prime}}{T}=\sqrt{\frac{6}{7}}\)
\(\Rightarrow T'=\sqrt{\frac{6}{7}} T\)
